# Dropdown outside-click

Every open dropdown, popover, or filter chip menu must collapse when the user clicks outside it.

## Required behavior

- While a dropdown is open, listen for `mousedown` (preferred) or `click` on `document`.
- If the event target is outside the dropdown root (trigger + menu), close it.
- Remove the listener when the dropdown closes or the component unmounts.
- Prefer implementing this inside the shared dropdown component (e.g. `FilterChipDropdown`, `DarkDropdown`) so every instance inherits it.

## Pattern

```jsx
const ref = useRef(null)

useEffect(() => {
  if (!open) return
  function handleOutside(e) {
    if (ref.current && !ref.current.contains(e.target)) {
      setOpen(false) // or onClose()
    }
  }
  document.addEventListener('mousedown', handleOutside)
  return () => document.removeEventListener('mousedown', handleOutside)
}, [open])

return (
  <div ref={ref} className="relative">
    {/* trigger + menu */}
  </div>
)
```

## Also

- Put the `ref` on a wrapper that contains both the trigger button and the menu panel.
- When opening one dropdown in a group, close the others.
- Do not leave dropdown open state only toggled by the trigger with no outside-click path.
